Subject: Backport missing <cstdint> includes from upstream PR #401 onto v0.11.0
Filename: dhi-trixie-gcc14-missing-cstdint.patch
DHI definition: package/main/opentelemetry-ebpf-reducer/debian-13/0.yaml (patch@v1)

v0.11.0 predates opentelemetry-network's Debian trixie/GCC 14 base bump. Two files
relied on <cstdint> being transitively included by libstdc++ headers that newer
libstdc++ (as shipped in trixie) no longer pulls in: util/string.inl uses uint*_t
types without including it directly, and the render_compiler code-generator
template (MessageGenerator.xtend) emits generated descriptor.cc files that use
uint16_t without it either. This is the exact upstream fix, backported verbatim
since it postdates the v0.11.0 tag.

Upstream PR: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-network/pull/401

diff --git a/util/string.inl b/util/string.inl
index 37c3d5a3..91ebe9d0 100644
--- a/util/string.inl
+++ b/util/string.inl
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 #include <type_traits>

 #include <cerrno>
-#include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstdint>

 template <typename T> bool integer_from_string(char const *in, T &out)
 {
diff --git a/renderc/io.opentelemetry.render/src/io/opentelemetry/render/generator/MessageGenerator.xtend b/renderc/io.opentelemetry.render/src/io/opentelemetry/render/generator/MessageGenerator.xtend
index 75c175a6..37046fb8 100644
--- a/renderc/io.opentelemetry.render/src/io/opentelemetry/render/generator/MessageGenerator.xtend
+++ b/renderc/io.opentelemetry.render/src/io/opentelemetry/render/generator/MessageGenerator.xtend
@@ -132,6 +132,7 @@ class MessageGenerator {
     «generatedCodeWarning()»

     #include "descriptor.h"
+    #include <cstdint>

     /***********************
      * DESCRIPTORS
